// Description: Detects execution of Windows Search URIs ("search:" / "search-ms:") spawned from common user-facing applications such as web browsers (Edge, Chrome, Firefox) or Microsoft Outlook, which may indicate phishing-driven execution, malicious shortcut activation, or abuse of Windows Search protocol handlers for remote resource redirection.
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1204.001, T1204.002, T1059
// Data Sources: DeviceProcessEvents
// Threat Actor: Common in phishing campaigns and social engineering attacks leveraging Windows Search URIs delivered via email or browser content; not attributed to a single actor.
// Severity: High
// False Positives: Legitimate enterprise use of search URIs in internal documentation portals, productivity tools, or helpdesk workflows involving Windows Search integration.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFileName in~
(
    "msedge.exe",
    "chrome.exe",
    "firefox.exe",
    "outlook.exe"
)
| where ProcessCommandLine has_any ("search:", "search-ms:")
| project
    Timestamp,
    DeviceName,
    AccountName,
    InitiatingProcessFileName,
    ProcessCommandLine
